          "collected_by": "Neil M Khosla",
          "collection_date": "2023-04-17",
          "description": {
            "comment": "The Golden Arrow Poison Frog (Phyllobates terribilis) is a species of poison frog native to the rainforests along the Pacific coast of Colombia. It stands out as a comparative species among poison frogs, notable for its color variation, behavioral plasticity, and toxin-sequestering capabilities. The sample described here comes from a female bred in captivity in the USA by Indoor Ecosystems. It was collected by Lauren O'Connell, Neil Khosla, and Aurora Alvarez-Buylla at Stanford University to create a high-quality reference genome, supporting research related to toxin sequestration, parental care, and the epigenetic modification of juvenile social behavior. Sequencing and genome assembly were carried out by Cantata Bio in Santa Cruz, California, and the data was further curated by Roberto Marquez at the University of Michigan.",
